<slt:ignore>


# pudge_view and deadinside depend on pudge. Duckdb's views and indexes keep the
# base column by name, so DependencyManager::AlterObject refuses RENAME COLUMN under
# a dependent (only index dependents are allowed through), the same refusal the
# table and view renames above pin. PG allows it because its dependents hold the
# column number.
statement error
ALTER TABLE pudge RENAME COLUMN a TO a_renamed;
----
db error: ERROR: Cannot alter entry "pudge" because there are entries that depend on it.
table macro function "clickclack" depends on table "pudge".
view "pudge_view" depends on table "pudge".
Drop the dependent entries first and recreate them after the change.


query
SELECT a FROM pudge;
----
a


statement error
ALTER TABLE pudge RENAME COLUMN nonexistent TO something;
----
db error: ERROR: Table "pudge" does not have a column with name "nonexistent"

Did you mean: "a"


